scene intro
  line "Wen Li-hsiang: \"I came to this country to build a railroad. Instead I learned to build a grave for every man who looked at me like I was less than human.\""
scene camp
  line "Wen Li-hsiang: \"The railroad paid us less than white men, gave us the dangerous powder work, and called it opportunity. I took their money and learned their weapons.\""
scene camp
  line "Wen Li-hsiang: \"In Los Angeles, they burned our homes in '71. The police watched. That is when I decided I would never be helpless again.\""
scene mission
  line "Wen Li-hsiang: \"I can handle a rifle. The question is whether you can handle fighting beside a Chinaman.\""
scene mission
  line "Wen Li-hsiang: \"I see movement behind those rocks. Two of them, maybe three.\""
